<!--
	Passive tree ACTIVE skills, granted by the ACTIVE_SKILL nodes in data/passivetree/*.xml
	(see PassiveTreeManager.applyAll). Ids 90400-90451 are the six archetype sectors (two
	each), 90460-90465 the six hybrid sectors (one each).

	Engine rules these follow (DocumentSkill / Skill / Formulas):
	  * Damage power is read from the skill (<power> as a direct child of <skill>), never from
	    inside a PhysicalDamage / MagicalDamage effect. Heal / ManaHeal / DamOverTime are the
	    opposite: their <power> goes inside the effect.
	  * Continuous effects (Buff, Debuff, Stun, Root, DamOverTime) are only applied by A2, A4
	    and DA2 skills, after the activateRate roll. An A1 skill only runs instant effects.
	  * A self Buff in <selfEffects> needs A3 (retail 409 Critical Blow).
	  * Damage, heal and debuff skills have 9 levels keyed to magicLevel 1/20/40/52/58/64/70/76/82.
	    With CalculateMagicSuccessBySkillMagicLevel the magic level decides magic hit and debuff
	    land chance, so a fixed low magic level would fail against high-level targets. Their
	    tree nodes use skillLevel="auto": the character gets the highest level whose magicLevel
	    it has reached, and moves up on level up. Power follows retail curves (36 Whirlwind for
	    physical, 1231 Aura Flare for magic). Pure buffs stay at one level.
	  * abnormalType NONE: recasting the same skill replaces it, and it stacks with every
	    retail buff. It still takes a buff slot.

	The client needs Skillname-e.dat / Skillgrp.dat rows for every id here, or it shows the
	skill without a name or icon. <icon> below is only used by server-side HTML.
-->
<list xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="../../xsd/skills.xsd">

